### Builder Baseline

After writing `{{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}`, make Builder source/setup edits into
a local baseline before any fix work starts:
```bash
cd {{ work_dir }}
git diff --no-color "$(cat {{ artifact_paths.base_commit_hash }})" > {{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}
if [ -s {{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }} ]; then
  git reset --hard "$(cat {{ artifact_paths.base_commit_hash }})"
  git apply --index {{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}
  git diff --cached --no-color > {{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}.staged
  cmp {{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }} {{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}.staged
  git -c user.name=arise-builder -c user.email=arise-builder@example.invalid commit -m arise-builder-baseline
  rm -f {{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}.staged
fi
```
- This commit is local runtime state, not a deliverable. It establishes the Builder-adjusted baseline so `{{ artifact_paths.model_patch }}` can contain only Fixer edits.
- A later repository-state check must reproduce `{{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}`
  byte-for-byte from the recorded Builder baseline.
- Do not use `git add -A`; it can commit untracked build outputs or generated files that `{{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}` cannot replay.
