### Validation Steps

{% include 'domains/secbench/phases/_detached_exec.j2' %}

Validate the build before continuing: the project compiles with the
`{{ sanitizer }}` sanitizer enabled and the instrumented binary actually
executes. Run `secb build` detached and poll its sentinel rather than
blocking one shell call on it:
{{ secb_build_validation(artifact_paths, phase_commands) }}
Once the build reports `exit=0`, read `{{ artifact_paths.binary_paths }}` and run
each declared binary with `--help` or `-h` when supported (short calls; no need
to detach them). Bound every smoke invocation with a short timeout and inspect its
actual output and exit status. A timeout is not evidence of successful initialization.
Every build, patch, exploit, and post-patch replay timeout remains a FAIL. If a binary fails
to load the sanitizer runtime
(e.g. "cannot open shared object file: libclang_rt.asan" or "libasan"), the
build is NOT complete — install the matching ASan runtime and fix
`LD_LIBRARY_PATH` until the instrumented binary runs. A build that compiles but
cannot execute is a FAIL. For a missing project library, use only one unambiguous,
project-local copy under `{{ work_dir }}`; missing, ambiguous, or path-escaping
candidates are a FAIL.
